{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-7c9aef35-ea42-4127-a13e-4af46163dcc4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e6309eb511dca86","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-xlim_tl5/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E005.md","content":"# Operator split-server topology for the dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance\n\n## Description\n\nExtend the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute — a split-server topology — and configure the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to that dedicated instance. The operator uses its existing Helm-in-operator pattern: the MLflow CR spec is converted to Helm values, rendered through embedded chart templates, and applied via Server-Side Apply. The main tracking server continues to handle experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry; the artifacts-only instance handles artifact serving with workspace validation.\n\n## Scope\n\n- New Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute.\n- Updates to the main tracking Deployment configuration to route artifact traffic to the dedicated instance, per the selected routing design from the artifact traffic routing investigation.\n- Propagation of workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration mechanisms the operator already uses for the main tracking deployment.\n- HTTPRoute resources created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n- Operator validation rejecting configurations where the artifacts-only instance lacks workspace flags while workspace-aware artifact serving is enabled (misconfiguration could otherwise let artifact requests bypass workspace validation).\n- Backwards compatibility: MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving reconcile unchanged.\n- The dedicated instance runs the workspace-aware artifacts-only server with the combined flag set (`--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`); the server image with that capability is consumed as a deployment configuration reference, coordinated at integration time rather than sequenced behind the server work.\n- The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar is deployed on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment (authentication layer unchanged).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Reconciling an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment.\n- The artifacts-only Deployment's container command includes `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`.\n- The main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance per the selected routing design.\n- An MLflow CR specifying the artifacts-only instance without workspace flags while workspace-aware artifact serving is enabled is rejected with a clear validation error.\n- MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving produce no artifacts-only resources and reconcile as before (backwards compatibility).\n- End-to-end through the deployed split topology: a workspace member's artifact request for an experiment in their workspace succeeds (HTTP 200 with correct artifact content), and a request for an experiment in another workspace is denied (HTTP 403).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P1] MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute.\n- [P1] Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":67957,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87bf0c123e428206","agent_id":"ad0c4515b2d0a7003","session_id":"52e2d593-99fe-4673-8bf8-9749f85fbc69","uuid":"6af5a1e9-fd7d-46b3-bbf5-a6e15c372bd4","timestamp":"2026-10-23T16:12:51.959Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
