{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84c1746d98c19052","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n3\ttitle: Investigate plugin workspace resolution dependencies in the artifacts-only\n4\t  context\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n6\tcomponent: MLflow\n7\tteam: MLflow Team\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Investigate plugin workspace resolution dependencies in the artifacts-only context\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tResolve whether the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution — workspace provider initialization and experiment-to-workspace mapping — can function in an MLflow artifacts-only server context where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The strategy flags this as a genuine unknown: if workspace resolution is currently coupled to the full tracking server initialization path, the plugin requires refactoring before workspace-aware artifact serving can work. The answer determines the scope and approach of the plugin extension work and of the server-side workspace provider initialization.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Analyze the plugin's workspace provider initialization path (registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) to identify any dependency on tracking store or model registry store initialization.\n35\t- Determine whether the `kubernetes://` workspace store provides experiment-to-workspace mapping that is accessible without initializing tracking stores.\n36\t- Build a minimal reproduction or test harness that exercises workspace resolution in an artifacts-only server context, with tracking and model registry stores uninitialized.\n37\t- If coupling is found: document the specific initialization dependencies and recommend a refactor approach that factors workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin.\n38\t- Record the bounded outcome: (A) workspace resolution is independent — verification and tests only; (B) workspace resolution is coupled to full server initialization — refactor required.\n39\t\n40\t## Acceptance Criteria\n41\t\n42\t- A written findings report states, with code-level evidence, whether workspace resolution initializes and resolves experiment-to-workspace mapping without tracking store or model registry store initialization.\n43\t- A runnable reproduction demonstrates workspace resolution succeeding or failing in the artifacts-only context (tracking and registry stores uninitialized).\n44\t- If coupling exists, the report enumerates each initialization dependency and recommends an independent-initialization refactor approach.\n45\t- The bounded outcome (independent vs coupled) is recorded together with the evidence that selects it.\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\t- [P1] Auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization — gating investigation: the outcome determines the scope and approach of the work delivering this requirement and of the workspace-aware artifact serving requirements below it.\n50\t- Strategy assumption \"the workspace store (`kubernetes://` URI scheme) provides experiment-to-workspace mapping accessible without initializing tracking stores — needs validation\" — resolved by this investigation.\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-918861ee198b169f","agent_id":"a259ae75130f24d6c","session_id":"52e2d593-99fe-4673-8bf8-9749f85fbc69","uuid":"8e3cec5a-649