{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb7241f45690c413","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n3\ttitle: Workspace-aware artifacts-only serving in the MLflow tracking server\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the investigation finds workspace resolution coupled to tracking\n16\t    store initialization, the workspace provider initialization approach in the server\n17\t    changes to accommodate the refactored independent initialization path.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Workspace-aware artifacts-only serving in the MLflow tracking server\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tMake the MLflow server's `--artifacts-only` mode composable with the existing `--enable-workspaces` flag, so the artifacts-only server initializes only the workspace provider needed to validate artifact requests. When both flags are set, the server requires an explicit `--workspace-store-uri`, resolves each artifact request's path to its parent experiment, looks up the experiment's workspace assignment via the workspace store, and delegates authorization to the existing auth plugin infrastructure. Requests failing workspace validation are denied with HTTP 403. The design is fail-closed: if the workspace store is unreachable while workspace-aware mode is active, requests are denied rather than served without validation. No new server flag is introduced.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Flag composition: allow `--artifacts-only` to combine with `--enable-workspaces`; require an explicit `--workspace-store-uri` when both are set (server fails to start with a clear error if it is missing).\n44\t- Initialize only the workspace provider in artifacts-only + workspaces mode; tracking stores and model registry stores stay uninitialized and non-artifact API endpoints remain disabled.\n45\t- Workspace validation of artifact requests: resolve the artifact path to its parent experiment (initial implementation scoped to the S3 artifact store's `{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/` path structure), look up the experiment's workspace assignment via the workspace store, and delegate authorization to the existing auth plugin infrastructure; denials return HTTP 403.\n46\t- Fail-closed behavior: with workspace-aware mode active and the workspace store unreachable, deny requests with HTTP 503 indicating workspace validation is unavailable; never serve artifacts without validation.\n47\t- Backwards compatibility: `--artifacts-only` without `--enable-workspaces` retains current behavior; single-tenant deployments and configurations without workspace flags are unchanged; no existing API contracts, CLI arguments, or configuration keys are removed or change meaning.\n48\t- Audit logging of workspace access denials in artifact serving through server logs.\n49\t- Document limitations for non-standard artifact roots (initial implementation scoped to the S3 artifact store, the standard RHOAI configuration).\n50\t- Measure per-request workspace validation overhead and document the result, informing the product decision on caching (performance optimization itself is out of scope for this strategy).\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- The server starts with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes://` and initializes only the workspace provider; tracking and model registry stores remain uninitialized and non-artifact API endpoints remain disabled.\n55\t- The server started with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces` but without `--workspace-store-uri` fails to start with a clear error message.\n56\t- A user who is a member of workspace A requesting an artifact belonging to an experiment in workspace A receives HTTP 200 with the correct artifact content.\n57\t- A user who is a member of workspace A but not workspace B requesting an artifact belonging to an experiment in workspace B receives HTTP 403 with an error message indicating insufficient workspace permissions.\n58\t- With the workspace store unreachable, artifact requests are denied with HTTP 503 indicating workspace validation is unavailable; no artifact is served without validation.\n59\t- With `--artifacts-only` set without `--enable-workspaces`, any authenticated user's artifact request is served without workspace validation (current behavior preserved, HTTP 200 regardless of workspace membership).\n60\t- Workspace access denials in artifact serving are recorded in server logs.\n61\t- Per-request workspace validation latency overhead is measured and documented.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- [P0] `--artifacts-only` can be combined with `--enable-workspaces` and `--workspace-store-uri` to enable workspace-validated artifact serving.\n66\t- [P0] Artifact requests through the workspace-aware artifacts-only server are validated against workspace membership; requests from users without workspace membership are denied with HTTP 403.\n67\t- [P0] Workspace-aware artifact serving is fail-closed: if the workspace store is unreachable, requests are denied.\n68\t- [P0] Single-tenant deployments and configurations without `--enable-workspaces` retain current behavior with no changes.\n69\t- [P2] Audit logging for workspace access denials in artifact serving through server logs (bundled with the P0 work: logged in the same artifact request-handling surface that enforces the 403 denials — same code path, endpoints, component and team; not a deferrable distinct feature).\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-918861ee198b169f","agent_id":"a259ae75130f24d6c","session_id":"52e2d593-99fe-4673-8bf8-9749f85fbc69","uuid":"08a0e626-2686-45aa-84bd-1cb8d79789a0","timestamp":"2026-10-23T16:15:10.799Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb7241f45690c413","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
