{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e15f85efc13dc70","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n3\ttitle: Investigate artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigate artifact traffic routing design for the split-server topology\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tDetermine how the MLflow operator should configure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server topology. The strategy flags this as an open question owned by the MLflow Team: the answer affects the HTTPRoute design and determines whether the tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations. The outcome selects between bounded alternatives and gates the operator's routing implementation.\n30\t\n31\t## Scope\n32\t\n33\t- Evaluate the bounded routing alternatives: (A) gateway-level routing via Gateway API HTTPRoute path/host rules directing artifact API traffic to the dedicated instance, with no tracking server change; (B) a tracking server configuration change to delegate artifact operations to the dedicated instance, wired by the operator.\n34\t- Assess HTTPRoute design implications: path matching for artifact endpoints, and interaction with the operator's existing conditional CRD discovery pattern for Gateway API.\n35\t- Determine whether the main tracking server or its deployment requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations, and what that configuration surface would be.\n36\t- Record a bounded recommendation with rationale and the evidence that selects it.\n37\t\n38\t## Acceptance Criteria\n39\t\n40\t- A written design recommendation documents the selected routing approach with rationale and an evaluation of the bounded alternatives.\n41\t- The recommendation explicitly states whether the tracking server requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations (outcome A: no server change; outcome B: server-side delegation configuration required).\n42\t- HTTPRoute design implications, including behavior under the operator's conditional Gateway API CRD discovery, are documented.\n43\t\n44\t## HLR Traceability\n45\t\n46\t- [P1] Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance — gating investigation: the outcome determines the design that delivers this requirement and whether additional server-side configuration work exists.\n47\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-918861ee198b169f","agent_id":"a259ae75130f24d6c","session_id":"52e2d593-99fe-4673-8bf8-9749f85fbc69","uuid":"bd4f018f-3083-4c46-8942-e88739c7ff85","timestamp":"2026-10-23T16:15:13.936Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e15f85efc13dc70","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
