{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3754d16973816d2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: Operator split-server topology for the dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the routing design investigation selects server-side delegation\n15\t    instead of gateway-level HTTPRoute routing, the operator's routing implementation\n16\t    and HTTPRoute design change accordingly and the main tracking deployment configuration\n17\t    work differs.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Operator split-server topology for the dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tExtend the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute — a split-server topology — and configure the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to that dedicated instance. The operator uses its existing Helm-in-operator pattern: the MLflow CR spec is converted to Helm values, rendered through embedded chart templates, and applied via Server-Side Apply. The main tracking server continues to handle experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry; the artifacts-only instance handles artifact serving with workspace validation.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- New Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute.\n44\t- Updates to the main tracking Deployment configuration to route artifact traffic to the dedicated instance, per the selected routing design from the artifact traffic routing investigation.\n45\t- Propagation of workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration mechanisms the operator already uses for the main tracking deployment.\n46\t- HTTPRoute resources created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n47\t- Operator validation rejecting configurations where the artifacts-only instance lacks workspace flags while workspace-aware artifact serving is enabled (misconfiguration could otherwise let artifact requests bypass workspace validation).\n48\t- Backwards compatibility: MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving reconcile unchanged.\n49\t- The dedicated instance runs the workspace-aware artifacts-only server with the combined flag set (`--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`); the server image with that capability is consumed as a deployment configuration reference, coordinated at integration time rather than sequenced behind the server work.\n50\t- The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar is deployed on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment (authentication layer unchanged).\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Reconciling an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment.\n55\t- The artifacts-only Deployment's container command includes `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`.\n56\t- The main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance per the selected routing design.\n57\t- An MLflow CR specifying the artifacts-only instance without workspace flags while workspace-aware artifact serving is enabled is rejected with a clear validation error.\n58\t- MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving produce no artifacts-only resources and reconcile as before (backwards compatibility).\n59\t- End-to-end through the deployed split topology: a workspace member's artifact request for an experiment in their workspace succeeds (HTTP 200 with correct artifact content), and a request for an experiment in another workspace is denied (HTTP 403).\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- [P1] MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute.\n64\t- [P1] Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-918861ee198b169f","agent_id":"a259ae75130f24d6c","session_id":"52e2d593-99fe-4673-8bf8-9749f85fbc69","uuid":"af9ab142-f890-40b9-8eee-cc1d9f9ae92a","timestamp":"2026-10-23T16:15:17.112Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3754d16973816d2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
