nals rationale files exist and their rationales match the frontmatter values.\n158\t\n159\tCalibration was verified against `.context` rather than taken on internal consistency\n160\talone:\n161\t\n162\t- `architecture_claims: +1` on all four Implementation epics, each citing a context\n163\t  file that actually corroborates the claim: mlflow.md documents the deployed CMD\n164\t  flag set (`--app-name kubernetes-auth --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri\n165\t  kubernetes:// --serve-artifacts`) and the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins v1.5.0 package;\n166\t  mlflow-operator.md documents the Helm-in-operator pattern, Server-Side Apply, and\n167\t  conditional Gateway API CRD discovery. This is the calibrated shape — no\n168\t  \"no architecture claims\" misses.\n169\t- `repo_access` values are honest and verified: E003/BRANCH-B-E006 cite\n170\t  red-hat-data-services/mlflow and E005 cites red-hat-data-services/mlflow-operator,\n171\t  both documented as repositories in the respective context files; E002 scores 0\n172\t  because mlflow.md documents the plugins package only as PyPI-installed with no\n173\t  source repository — accurate.\n174\t- Investigation signals are consistent with the rubric's polarity and conditions:\n175\t  both questions are specific with defined selection criteria (+1), answers are\n176\t  determinable from readable source (+1 source_accessibility — correctly scoring the\n177\t  operator's generated templates as source per the rubric note), end-to-end\n178\t  verification needs a live cluster (local_runnability 0, cluster_hardware_dependence\n179\t  -1 for peripheral-only dependence), and no stakeholder decision gates either\n180\t  question (human_judgment_required 0).\n181\t\n182\tBRANCH-B-E006's lower change_specificity/pattern_precedent/adapter_pattern scores (0)\n183\twith the gated-scope rationale are appropriately calibrated for an epic whose\n184\tconcrete surface is unknown until the investigation selects it.\n185\t\n186\t### 6. Accepta