e explicit\n218\tdispositions in the summary's Unknowns table (two resolved by investigations, two\n219\tconverted to health warnings with measurement ACs, the rest to epic ACs); all four\n220\tstrategy risks surface in epic scope or health warnings (plugin coupling → E001,\n221\tpath-resolution complexity → E003 scope, split-topology misconfiguration → E005's\n222\tvalidation AC, per-request latency → E003 measurement AC + health warning). The SME\n223\toverrides (no new flag, split deployment not config toggle, SSAR de-specified) are\n224\tlogged and visibly honored in the epic scopes. Integration testing from the effort\n225\testimate is distributed as end-to-end ACs on E003 and E005 covering multi-tenant,\n226\tbackwards-compatibility, single-tenant, fail-closed, and split-routing scenarios.\n227\t\n228\tConditional branches cover both bounded outcomes of E004: outcome A is delivered\n229\tentirely within E005's routing scope (no branch epic, correctly), outcome B by\n230\tBRANCH-B-E006 with `gate_failure_impact.action=remove`. Docs-authoring: the strategy's\n231\tPrerequisites list `Documentation Support: _Pending human review_`, not `Yes`, so no\n232\tdocs-authoring epic is required — the summary's Health Warning 6 documents this\n233\treasoning, including why no design-doc epic was generated.\n234\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc762b36544567a2","agent_id":"a4b47c329fafc8d7d","session_id":"52e2d593-99fe-4673-8bf8-9749f85fbc69","uuid":"6dafa711-5ff9-4175-9102-1848b4fce73e","timestamp":"2026-10-23T16:21:21.288Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8dff755cfb3b9ef","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
