{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-850fc9f02470a955","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n3\ttitle: Extend plugin workspace resolution for the artifacts-only server context\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the investigation finds workspace resolution coupled to full\n15\t    tracking server initialization, the epic expands to factor resolution into an\n16\t    independent initialization path within the plugin; if independent, the epic shrinks\n17\t    to verification and tests.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 0\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Extend plugin workspace resolution for the artifacts-only server context\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tVerify and extend the mlflow-kubernetes-plugins auth plugin so that workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only MLflow server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The artifacts-only proxy calls the same workspace resolution logic the tracking server already uses for non-artifact operations, before proxying artifact requests to the storage backend. The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` authentication setup are unchanged.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Verify workspace resolution (workspace provider initialization, experiment-to-workspace lookup) in the artifacts-only server context, per the outcome of the workspace-resolution dependency investigation.\n44\t- If the investigation finds coupling to the full tracking server initialization path: factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin.\n45\t- Ensure resolution failures (for example, an unreachable workspace store) surface as errors rather than silent successes, so the server can enforce fail-closed behavior.\n46\t- Preserve existing workspace resolution behavior for the tracking server's non-artifact operations (no regression).\n47\t- Unit and integration tests covering workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Workspace resolution initializes and resolves experiment-to-workspace mapping in an artifacts-only context with tracking and model registry stores uninitialized, demonstrated by passing tests.\n52\t- Existing workspace resolution tests for the tracking server context pass unchanged (no regression to non-artifact operations).\n53\t- Workspace store unavailability during resolution produces an error result, not a successful or undefined response.\n54\t- Any refactor keeps the plugin's registration surface (`mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group, `WorkspaceStoreRegistry` loading) compatible with the tracking server's existing usage.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- [P1] Auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization.\n59\t- Prerequisite of the P0 requirements for workspace-validated artifact serving and fail-closed behavior in the artifacts-only server.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8002fd48c04a1865","agent_id":"ac37617e9c63bf965","session_id":"52e2d593-99fe-4673-8bf8-9749f85fbc69","uuid":"b332e853-b4e5-4411-8737-2bfd6c912965","timestamp":"2026-10-23T16:25:54.133Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-850fc9f02470a955","permission_decision"