{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-868a34eb69ae6fe9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: Operator deployment of the dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Operator deployment of the dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tExtend the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute — the deployment half of the split-server topology. The operator uses its existing Helm-in-operator pattern: the MLflow CR spec is converted to Helm values, rendered through embedded chart templates, and applied via Server-Side Apply. The dedicated instance runs the workspace-aware artifacts-only server; the main tracking server continues to handle experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry. This epic delivers the dedicated instance's resources only — configuring the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to the instance is a separate epic that depends on the artifact traffic routing design investigation.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- New Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute.\n38\t- Propagation of workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration mechanisms the operator already uses for the main tracking deployment.\n39\t- HTTPRoute resources created conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies.\n40\t- Operator validation rejecting configurations where the artifacts-only instance lacks workspace flags while workspace-aware artifact serving is enabled (misconfiguration could otherwise let artifact requests bypass workspace validation).\n41\t- Backwards compatibility: MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving reconcile unchanged.\n42\t- The dedicated instance runs the workspace-aware artifacts-only server with the combined flag set (`--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`); the server image with that capability is consumed as a deployment configuration reference, coordinated at integration time rather than sequenced behind the server work.\n43\t- The kube-rbac-proxy sidecar is deployed on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment (authentication layer unchanged).\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- Reconciling an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment.\n48\t- The artifacts-only Deployment's container command includes `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts`.\n49\t- An MLflow CR specifying the artifacts-only instance without workspace flags while workspace-aware artifact serving is enabled is rejected with a clear validation error.\n50\t- MLflow CRs without split-server artifact serving produce no artifacts-only resources and reconcile as before (backwards compatibility).\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- [P1] MLflow operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8002fd48c04a1865","agent_id":"ac37617e9c63bf965","session_id":"52e2d593-99fe-4673-8bf8-9749f85fbc69","uuid":"bb4ee241-e226-4c1d-bcb1-038d93b0018e","timestamp":"2026-10-23T16:26:03.819Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-868a34eb69ae6fe9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009"}
