{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac01012cfdfb072b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E007\n3\ttitle: Operator configuration of artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E004\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the routing design investigation selects server-side delegation\n16\t    instead of gateway-level HTTPRoute routing, the routing implementation on the\n17\t    main tracking deployment changes accordingly and is wired to the server-side\n18\t    delegation configuration surface instead of HTTPRoute rules.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 5\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Operator configuration of artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tConfigure the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance — the routing half of the operator's split-server topology. The routing approach is determined by the artifact traffic routing design investigation: either gateway-level routing via Gateway API HTTPRoute path/host rules directing artifact API traffic to the dedicated instance (no tracking server change), or a tracking server configuration change to delegate artifact operations, set on the main tracking deployment by the operator's rendering. This epic implements the selected routing design in the operator, building on the dedicated artifacts-only instance deployment.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Updates to the main tracking Deployment configuration to route artifact traffic to the dedicated instance, per the selected routing design from the artifact traffic routing investigation.\n45\t- Under the gateway-level routing outcome: HTTPRoute path/host rules directing artifact API traffic to the dedicated instance's Service, consistent with the operator's conditional Gateway API CRD discovery pattern.\n46\t- Under the server-side delegation outcome: operator rendering of the main tracking deployment that sets the tracking server's delegation configuration (the configuration surface itself is delivered by the routing-design branch, not this epic).\n47\t- Verification that artifact requests through the main tracking deployment's ingress reach the dedicated artifacts-only instance and non-artifact API traffic continues to reach the main tracking server.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- The main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance per the selected routing design.\n52\t- Artifact API requests entering through the main tracking deployment's ingress are served by the dedicated artifacts-only instance, and non-artifact API requests continue to be served by the main tracking server.\n53\t- Where the selected routing design requires a server-side delegation configuration, the operator's rendering of the main tracking deployment sets that configuration.\n54\t- End-to-end through the deployed split topology: a workspace member's artifact request for an experiment in their workspace succeeds (HTTP 200 with correct artifact content), and a request for an experiment in another workspace is denied (HTTP 403).\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- [P1] Main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance.\n59\t"}]}